                "authorType": "COMMENT",
                "competitionRanking": 492,
                "content": "<p>My comment wasn't complete. I meant to say vLLM with trl's colocate mode: they occupy the same memory, and vLLM releases memory when it stops generating, allowing trl's trainer to proceed (and vice versa). <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/blog/vllm-colocate\" target=\"_blank\">From this blogpost.</a></p>",
